## Output contract

Wrap your ENTIRE reply in a single ```json … ``` fence and nothing else — no
prose, no second fence, nothing before or after the fence. Use plain ASCII
double quotes, never smart quotes.

The top level must have EXACTLY two keys: `format` and `sentences`. Return every
input `id` exactly once, and only those ids. Each entry in `sentences` has:

  - id            the exact id from the input (required)
  - romanisation  full-sentence romanisation
  - english       natural English translation
  - literal       word-for-word gloss: one English word per {{script}} token, in
                  token order; hyphenate multi-word glosses (कितने -> "how-many")
  - register      EXACTLY one of: informal | standard | formal
  - breakdown     one entry per {{script}} word, in order; each entry:
                    surface  the word in {{script}}
                    roman    its romanisation
                    gloss    short English gloss
                    kind     optional part of speech (noun, verb, pronoun, …)

## Example (shape only — do not copy these values)

```json
{
  "format": "lingo.enrich/v1",
  "sentences": [
    {
      "id": "sen-0001",
      "romanisation": "kaise ho Pratāp?",
      "english": "How are you, Pratap?",
      "literal": "how are Pratap",
      "register": "informal",
      "breakdown": [
        { "surface": "कैसे",   "roman": "kaise",  "gloss": "how",    "kind": "adverb" },
        { "surface": "हो",     "roman": "ho",     "gloss": "are",    "kind": "verb" },
        { "surface": "प्रताप", "roman": "Pratāp", "gloss": "Pratap", "kind": "noun" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

Return every id you were given, and only those ids. The input sentences follow.
